  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the man experiencing dating rejection",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man, who embodies the experience of going on a date and getting stood up. The man's resigned, frustrated expression and body language (hand on face, eyes closed) are culturally understood as symbols of disappointment and emotional letdown, which are central to the meme's narrative. The user identifies with this emotional state, projecting themselves onto the man as a representation of their own potential experience of dating rejection. This projection is implicit, as there are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you' in the text, but the universal relatability of the scenario and the man's universal expression create a strong implicit identification.",
